l,"_gate_accruals":0.0913938660172118,"_gp_accruals":false,"_score_accruals":4.6,"_gate_rev_volatility":0.30051200083489166,"_gp_rev_volatility":false,"_score_rev_volatility":28.4,"_gate_margin_vs_hist":0.02575718410287145,"_gp_margin_vs_hist":true,"_score_margin_vs_hist":67.8,"_gate_piotroski":6,"_gp_piotroski":false,"_score_piotroski":66.7,"_gate_spread":null,"_gp_spread":null,"_score_spread":null,"_gate_roic_consistency":null,"_gp_roic_consistency":null,"_score_roic_consistency":null,"_gate_incr_roic":null,"_gp_incr_roic":null,"_score_incr_roic":null,"_gate_margin_advantage":null,"_gp_margin_advantage":null,"_score_margin_advantage":null,"_gate_pool_share":null,"_gp_pool_share":null,"_score_pool_share":null,"_gate_rev_durability":0.15957174549397402,"_gp_rev_durability":true,"_score_rev_durability":100.0,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":null,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":null,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":null,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.0,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":false,"_score_shrhldr_yield":11.1,"_gate_share_shrink":0.014061336383317746,"_gp_share_shrink":false,"_score_share_shrink":32.4,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.026363883707859134,"_gp_sbc_dilution":false,"_score_sbc_dilution":56.1,"_gate_insider_own":0.19009,"_gp_insider_own":true,"_score_insider_own":100.0,"_gate_insider_buying":null,"_gp_insider_buying":null,"_score_insider_buying":null,"pf":[],"description_full":"LendingTree, Inc., through its subsidiary, operates online consumer platform in the United States. The company operates through three segments: Home, Consumer, and Insurance. The Home segments offer purchase mortgage, refinance mortgage, and home equity loans and lines of credit. The Consumer segment provides credit cards; personal, small business, and auto loans; deposit accounts; and other credit products, such as debt settlement services. The Insurance segment includes information, tools, and access to insurance quote products, including automobile, home, life, and health and Medicare through which consumers are matched with insurance lead aggregators to obtain insurance offers and policies. This segment also offers QuoteWizard, a marketplace for insurance comparison; and ValuePenguin, a personal finance website that offers consumers objective analysis on various financial topics. The company was formerly known as Tree.com, Inc. and changed its name to LendingTree, Inc. in January 2015. LendingTree, Inc. was incorporated in 1996 and is based in Charlotte, North Carolina.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Scott  Peyree | CEO, President & Director | Age 48 | Compensation: $1.0M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 919 people. Revenue per employee of $1.2M ranks in the top quartile among Financial Services peers, with revenue growing 24%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $66K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $32K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 1\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (6/10).","financial_summary":["LendingTree, Inc. is a small-cap financial services business with a $502M market cap on $1.1B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +4% over the past three years and +16% annually across the full decade, which puts it in mature, slow-growth territory. Operating margins are expanding by +8.4pp year-over-year, which is one of the strongest signals that the moat is deepening.","Returns on capital run at 1% against a 10% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests, with gross margins sitting at 37%.","The business throws off $61M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 5 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders. Cash conversion is thin at 0.48\u00d7, however, which raises the oldest question in analysis: are these earnings backed by cash?.","Accruals are elevated at +9.1% of assets, and Sloan showed firms building earnings through accruals rather than cash systematically underperform.","On the balance sheet, debt is moderate at 3.8\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, serviceable in normal conditions but worth watching through a downturn, and thin 1.7\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 19% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is, and profit capture is only 0.2\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (1.0) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Beneish M-Score flags potential earnings manipulation \u2014 a question of whether the reported numbers can be trusted","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Operating margins 23% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Accruals running hot at +9.1% of assets \u2014 earnings quality bears watching","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 7.0% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Value-trap profile (score 53/100): leveraged balance sheet under pressure; durably derated by the market \u2014 cheapness may reflect deterioration, not mispricing","sev":"amber","cat":"value_trap"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Shares offer a 21% margin of safety against estimated fair value","Valued at a 37% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Analyzing Navient (NASDAQ:NAVI) & LendingTree (NASDAQ:TREE)","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/12/analyzing-navient-nasdaqnavi-lendingtree-nasdaqtree.html","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794510931.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.869,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"LendingTree, Inc. (NASDAQ:TREE) Stock Has Average Price Target of $53.60 According to Analysts","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/12/lendingtree-inc-nasdaqtree-stock-has-average-price-target-of-53-60-according-to-analysts.html","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794466738.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.511,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["analyst_action"]},{"title":"LendingTree (NASDAQ:TREE) Shares Gap Up \u2013 What\u2019s Next?","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/06/lendingtree-nasdaqtree-shares-gap-up-whats-next.html","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793977268.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.934,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Why are LendingTree (TREE) shares soaring today","source":"stockstory.org","link":"https://stockstory.org/us/stocks/nasdaq/tree/news/why-up-down/why-are-lendingtree-tree-shares-soaring-today","date":"2026-11-04","timestamp":1793817941.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.527,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Automax.ai Wins Innovation Challenge at LendingTree's 2026 Lender Summit","source":"prnewswire.com","link":"https://www.prnewswire.com/news-releases/automaxai-wins-innovation-challenge-at-lendingtrees-2026-lender-summit-302933909.html","date":"2026-11-09",